From 6ef44ef3033f56bae8c08c96e9da74ddf2a5748f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:57:31 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/60] Server hooks for a model family's own chat rules.

family.zig is an optional vtable a family installs in place of the chat template: prompt rendering, thinking and
effort fields, a streaming reply reader that parses its own call markup, and the turn it remembers. Without a
family the server runs as before.

chat.zig's reply collection moves to chat_generation.zig and openai.zig's run to openai_run.zig (pure moves), so
neither file passes 600 lines with the hooks in.

(cherry picked from commit 96ae8658371704822c70bbc05d50c51e35b7e378)
